# NestedText v3 - docbook/ per-folder DETAIL pass (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/docbook/ - 169 files, 8.6 MB
# Six versions 4.2 to 5.1. Second of the F18-rest detail passes; pattern
# follows tei.duo.nt and xhtml11.nt: folder shape, then mechanisms with
# release bindings, nothing invented.

folder-shape:
    versions: 4.2 29 files, 4.3 33 files, 4.4 31 files, 4.5 30 files, 5.0 17 files, 5.1 16 files
    four-x: dtd plus ent directories, DocBook XML without namespaces
    five-0: dtd 202992 B in 2 files, rng 1607011 B in 7, sch 17344 B in 1, xsd 762014 B in 3, docbook.nvdl at root, tools 46022 B in 2
    five-1: rng 3981566 B in 8, sch 53934 B in 4, docbook.nvdl at root, tools 51022 B in 2, no dtd directory

multi-schema-publishing-measured:
    > 5.0 ships five grammars for one vocabulary: dtd, rng, sch, xsd and
    > nvdl side by side. 5.1 drops the dtd directory and more than doubles
    > the rng to 3981566 bytes: the RELAX NG grammar is the maintained one
    > and the DTD is the legacy emission, the reverse of the 4.x shape.
    > Strongest in-corpus witness, beside TEI ODD, that one vocabulary
    > carries many grammars and the hand-kept one wins.

version-migration:
    > 4.x to 5.0 is a namespace migration with a grammar change on top:
    > DocBook 5 is namespaced, 4.x is not, so no 4.x document validates
    > under 5.x without rewriting. The 4.2-to-4.5 run (29/33/31/30 files)
    > is accretion inside one shape; 5.0 is a new shape that still ships
    > the old grammar beside the new ones for exactly one minor.

release-binding:
    > Stream 17 (429-file tree): DocBook 5.1 dropping dtd/ while doubling
    > rng/ is the precedent for retiring an emission without retiring the
    > vocabulary; the triple per artifact may likewise drop a form and keep
    > the source. Stream 9 (corpus convergence): the 4.x ent layering feeds
    > the shared-entity discipline beside DAISY.
